{%- comment -%}
  Trailing cursor dot — rendered from layout/theme.liquid.

  A snippet configured from Theme settings -> Cursor, not a section: it belongs
  to the layout rather than to any one template, exactly as the preloader does.
  A static section rendered from theme.liquid would show up in the section list
  of whichever template the merchant happened to be editing, reading as though
  the cursor belonged to the home page.

  Opting an element in is one attribute, anywhere in the theme:

    <a data-cursor>...</a>                      the disc, with the label below
    <a data-cursor data-cursor-label="Add">...  the disc, with its own wording

  The element is rendered on every device. bf-cursor.js never activates it
  without a pointer that can hover, so on a phone it stays at opacity 0 and
  binds no listeners — cheaper than asking Liquid to guess at the device, which
  it cannot do anyway.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if settings.cursor_enabled -%}
  {{ 'bf-cursor.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <script src="{{ 'bf-cursor.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

  {%- comment -%}
    aria-hidden, and no live region. The dot is a visual echo of the pointer;
    a screen reader user already knows what they are pointing at, and the label
    duplicates the link text the card announces anyway.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <bf-cursor class="cursor" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="cursor__follow">
      <div class="cursor__dot">
        <span class="cursor__label">{{ settings.cursor_label }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </bf-cursor>
{%- endif -%}
